<h1>Backfill historical data</h1>
<p>When you set up a new pipeline, you often want to load historical data that already exists in your source system. This recipe shows how to configure your pipeline to replay data from the past without disrupting real-time event flow.</p>

<h2>The pattern</h2>
<p>Backfilling typically involves two phases:</p>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Batch load:</strong> Query your source system for all historical records within a date range.</li>
  <li><strong>Stream events:</strong> Once historical data catches up, switch to real-time event streaming for ongoing updates.</li>
</ol>

<p>Godzilla pipelines support both approaches through the same connectors and destination configuration, so you can use one pipeline for both historical and real-time data.</p>

